  "final_answer": "All four deliverables are written and verified in `/app`:\n\n- **`collateral_audit.csv`** \u2014 60 in-scope items, columns `item_id,finding` (findings `|`-joined; clean items `none`).\n- **`zone_summary.csv`** \u2014 8 zones with the six required columns; `ZONE_ALLOWANCE_BREACH` on ZN-03, ZN-07, ZN-08, else `none`.\n- **`collateral_memo.md`** \u2014 memo to the safety office (review as of 2026-08-20; out-of-scope items; every flagged item with its deciding record; cleared items; zones over allowance; heightened inspection).\n- **`results.json`** \u2014 the eleven \u00a77 figures, all JSON numbers.\n\nKey results:\n- 60 in-scope audited (6 out of scope: 4 `standalone_graphic`, 2 `vehicle_wrap`).\n- 20 `PERMIT_NUMBER_MISSING` (pulled), 8 `EGRESS_MARKER_OBSTRUCTED`, 13 `OVERSIZE_COLLATERAL`; 21 compliant, 39 flagged, 41 findings total.\n- Three zones breach \u00a75 (ZN-03 50.5/40.0, ZN-07 93.5/90.0, ZN-08 48.0/45.0) \u2192 **heightened inspection in force**, tightening the \u00a74 cap by 1 sq ft in those zones and adding five oversize findings (COL-15, COL-16, COL-42, COL-48, COL-50).\n\nThe main traps the standard warns about: scope is read off type, not numbers (the six out-of-scope items); the governing permit follows the supersession chain (PMT-1004\u21921005\u21921006 narrows to ZN-03; PMT-1008 expires PMT-1007); and `valid_until` 2026-08-20 is still current while 2026-08-19 is not.",
